From: airoha-port <airoha@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: fix NULL deref in phy_leds_unregister on attach failure

struct phy_device has a "leds" list under CONFIG_LED_TRIGGER_PHY, but
phy_device_create() never initialises it.  When phy_attach_direct()
later fails (e.g. phy_init_hw() returns an error) the error path calls
phy_detach() -> phy_leds_unregister(), which walks that list and
dereferences a NULL pointer, panicking the kernel.

Initialise the list when the device is created.

Signed-off-by: airoha-port <airoha@local>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/phy_device.c	2026-10-09 19:16:15.849948998 +0800
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/phy_device.c	2026-10-09 19:16:15.853949471 +0800
@@ -630,6 +630,9 @@
 
 	dev->state = PHY_DOWN;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_LED_TRIGGER_PHY
+	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&dev->leds);
+#endif
 	mutex_init(&dev->lock);
 	INIT_DELAYED_WORK(&dev->state_queue, phy_state_machine);
 
